    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1284">

                <pb facs="1240" n="1074" sameAs="frus:frus1917/pg1074"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 312.115/310</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Collector Cobb to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">El Paso</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-06-20T12:00:00-07:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 20, 1917, noon</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Informed confidentially by party whose agent at Chihuahua was approached that
                    Chihuahua Government authorities are calling for forced loan of twenty-five
                    thousand dollars. This in spite of the fact that they have money on deposit in
                    El Paso. My June 19, noon.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d1284-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cobb</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
